<<
/Author (Hunter Hughes)
/CreationDate (D\07220261121175219\05505\04700\047)
/Creator (H Heuristics)
/Keywords (pattern formation\054 creation structures\054 recurrence of form\054 symmetry\054 phyllotaxis\054 golden angle\054 packing and tiling\054 fractals\054 branching networks\054 reaction\055diffusion\054 self\055organisation\054 convergent evolution)
/ModDate (D\07220261121175219\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (Across the natural world\054 strikingly similar patterns appear in systems that differ enormously in scale\054 material and history\056 Spirals recur in sunflowers\054 seashells\054 hurricanes and galaxies\073 hexagons in honeycombs\054 basalt columns\054 soap froth\054 living tissue and the atomic lattice of graphene\073 branching networks in trees\054 rivers\054 lungs\054 blood vessels and lightning\073 and unrelated animal lineages repeatedly arrive at the same eyes and streamlined bodies\056 This report asks why creation keeps producing the same forms across systems that seem to have nothing in common\056 It uses the word creation in the sense of generation\054 the production of form by processes\054 and states that its scientific argument neither requires nor excludes any view about the ultimate origin of the laws themselves\056)
/Title (Patterns in Creation\072 Why Similar Forms Recur Across Galaxies\054 Shells\054 Cells and Species\072 Constraint\054 Generation and Selection in the Architecture of Nature)
/Trapped /False
>>
